configure.ac: allow cross builds for Haiku

configure refuses a cross build for a host it does not name in its _host_ident cases (the
_PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM suffix): Haiku is in the first list (ac_sys_system, from HaikuPorts'
patchset) but not in this one. With it, _PYTHON_HOST_PLATFORM is haiku-aarch64, the platform tag of
the extension modules and of _sysconfigdata__haiku_aarch64-*.

HaikuPorts builds natively and never takes this path. Applied after HaikuPorts'
python3.14-3.14.8.patchset by scripts/build-python.sh, which regenerates configure with autoconf.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -810,6 +810,9 @@
 	*-*-vxworks*)
 		_host_ident=$host_cpu
 		;;
+	*-*-haiku*)
+		_host_ident=$host_cpu
+		;;
 	*-*-emscripten)
 		_host_ident=$(emcc -dumpversion | cut -f1 -d-)-$host_cpu
 		;;
